          "literatureReview": "Iron Studies panel provides comprehensive evaluation of iron metabolism. Serum iron reflects circulating iron, normal range 50-170 µg/dL. TIBC (Total Iron Binding Capacity) measures transferrin's iron-binding capacity, normal 250-450 µg/dL. Transferrin saturation (%) = (Iron/TIBC) × 100, normal 15-50%. Low iron with high TIBC suggests iron deficiency. Normal/low iron with normal TIBC suggests anemia of chronic disease. High iron with low TIBC suggests iron overload. Colorimetric methods provide accurate measurement. Used in diagnosis of iron deficiency anemia, hemochromatosis, and monitoring iron therapy. Best interpreted with ferritin levels for complete iron status assessment."
